Review this telemetry summarizer. Context: events can include failed and completed attempts; native_total inputTokens is a cumulative snapshot; settings_updated is only settings acceptance; mismatched actual models must remain visible. Identify every independent defect in this code, no speculative findings. Return exactly JSON {"findings":[codes]}, no Markdown. Allowed codes: CONFIRM_FROM_SETTINGS, FILTER_EXPECTED_MODEL, SUM_CUMULATIVE, DROP_FAILED_ATTEMPTS, RAW_SECRET_PERSISTENCE, NATIVE_BOUNDARY_BYPASS, UNBOUNDED_NETWORK, DUPLICATE_JSON_KEYS. Source:
def summarize(events, expected_model):
    usage = 0
    confirmed = False
    for event in events:
        if event.get('status') != 'completed':
            continue
        if event.get('event') == 'settings_updated':
            confirmed = True
        if event.get('model') != expected_model:
            continue
        if event.get('event') == 'native_total':
            usage += event['inputTokens']
    return {'usage': usage, 'confirmed': confirmed}
Do not use tools.
